    ["这是……狼鱼罐头的味道！谁在吃这个？ 不知道今天码头有格尔曼主题活动吗，扰乱秩序！"] = "This is... the smell of wolf fish canned food! Who is eating this? Don't they know there's a Gehrman-themed event at the dock today? Disturbing the order!",
    ["邓恩·史密斯，廷根市值夜者小队队长，性格沉稳，灰色的眼睛深邃冷静，就像古老森林里乏人问津的湖泊。\n队员们总笑话他健忘，有交代不完的事。可他记得每一个队员的名字，每一段并肩的过往。\n值夜者，守护黑夜之人，行走于安静的夜晚，战斗在大众看不到的地方，对抗着危险，彼此守护着对方的后背。\n邓恩舍不得他们。\n小伊特第一次出任务，吓得当场崩溃；阿德莱德曾替他挡下诅咒；道恩总爱用文字记下每个人的故事；科恩黎比伦纳德更像一个诗人，会在巡逻间隙弹起七弦琴，让琴声在廷根潮湿的夜风里飘散……这些人，这些事，邓恩一件都没忘。\n他做了一个在非凡者看来近乎疯狂的决定——将牺牲队员的非凡特性逐一服食，让他们的灵魂以另一种形式继续留在他身边。\n“这是一个自私的决定。”他曾对克莱恩说，“我并不确定……这是否是他们想要的。”\n可他一向如此。把所有人的悲伤扛在自己肩上，将队员牢牢护在身后。\n因此，面对无法战胜的敌人，他依然选择了守护。那时，他望向克莱恩，露出了一如往昔的温和笑容，就像每次任务结束后，他站在黑荆棘窗边，对归来的队员说“辛苦了”时一样。\n当廷根的黎明到来时，他已成为了那道光的一部分。"] = "Dunn Smith, captain of the Tingen Nighthawks, had a steady personality. His gray eyes were deep and calm, like an unfrequented lake in an ancient forest.\n His teammates always joked about his forgetfulness and how he had endless things to remind them of. But he remembered the name of every teammate and every past they had shared.\n Nighthawks, guardians of the night, walking in the quiet night, fighting in places the public could not see, confronting danger, and guarding each other's backs.\n Dunn could not bear to let them go.\n When Little Ite went on his first mission, he collapsed in terror; Adelaide had once blocked a curse for him; Dawn always loved to record everyone's stories in writing; Kenley was more like a poet than Leonard, playing the lyre during patrols and letting the music drift into the damp night wind of Tingen... Dunn had not forgotten a single one of these people or these events.\n He made a decision that seemed almost insane to other Beyonders—to consume the Beyonder characteristics of his sacrificed teammates one by one, allowing their souls to remain by his side in another form.\n \"This is a selfish decision,\" he once told Klein. \"I'm not sure... if this is what they wanted.\"\n But he had always been this way. Carrying everyone's sadness on his own shoulders, keeping his teammates firmly behind him.\n Therefore, facing an invincible enemy, he still chose to guard them. At that moment, he looked at Klein and revealed the same gentle smile as always, just like when he stood by the Blackthorn window after every mission and said \"Thank you for your hard work\" to the returning team.\n When the dawn of Tingen arrived, he had already become a part of that light.",
    ["邓恩队长，值夜者平时要做哪些工作？"] = "Captain Dunn, what kind of work do Nighthawks usually do?",
